---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "2026-07-30";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Paw Watch"
  description="Paw Watch privacy policy. What we collect, how we use it, and your rights."
>
  <section class="wrap-narrow prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      Paw Watch ("we," "our," or "the app") is published by Cerminara
      Consulting LLC, a Virginia-based independent consulting practice.
      This policy explains what information Paw Watch collects, how we
      use it, who we share it with, and the choices you have. We
      designed Paw Watch to collect the minimum data needed to make
      dog-walking safer — and nothing else.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>

    <h3>Account information</h3>
    <p>
      When you sign in, we receive your name and email from your sign-in
      provider — either Apple (Sign in with Apple) or Google (Sign in
      with Google). We use your display name to attribute reports to
      you and to greet you in the app. We do not receive your Apple ID
      password or your Google password.
    </p>

    <h3>Location data</h3>
    <p>
      With your permission, Paw Watch uses your device's location to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Verify your neighborhood.</strong> On first launch, we
        use your location once to confirm you live in the area you say
        you do. We do not store this location on your profile.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Tag the reports you submit.</strong> When you tap
        "Report a hazard," we attach your current latitude and longitude
        to the report so other walkers can see where it happened.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Show nearby hazards on the map.</strong> We use your
        location to fetch hazards within walking distance.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Track walks.</strong> If you start a walk, we record
        GPS points at regular intervals so you can review the route and
        distance afterward. You can end a walk at any time; the data
        stays on your device and only the start/end timestamps are
        saved to your account if you sign in.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Send you alerts.</strong> If you've set a home radius,
        we compare new reports to your saved location and notify you
        when a hazard appears within your radius.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can disable location at any time in iOS Settings. Paw Watch
      will continue to work for any features that don't require it.
    </p>

    <h3>Push notification tokens</h3>
    <p>
      If you grant notification permission, we receive a token from
      Apple/Google that lets us send you push notifications. We store
      this token on your profile and delete it when you sign out.
    </p>

    <h3>Photos (v1.0 ships without photo upload)</h3>
    <p>
      The current version of Paw Watch does not let you upload photos
      of hazards. The information we collect is limited to text
      descriptions, categories, and severity levels. A future version
      may add photo upload — if so, we'll update this policy before
      shipping.
    </p>

    <h3>Crash and performance data</h3>
    <p>
      We do not currently use a third-party crash reporter. If we add
      one (e.g., Sentry, Crashlytics), we'll update this policy and
      ask for your consent again.
    </p>

    <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your contacts list</li>
      <li>Your photos or camera (beyond what you explicitly upload)</li>
      <li>Your advertising identifier (IDFA)</li>
      <li>Your purchase history</li>
      <li>Your browsing history outside the app</li>
      <li>Your microphone or audio</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use your data</h2>
    <p>
      We use the data above to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Show you hazards reported by other walkers in your area</li>
      <li>Attribute reports and ratings to their authors</li>
      <li>Send you push notifications when you have alerts enabled</li>
      <li>Track your walks if you choose to use the walk feature</li>
      <li>Improve the app's reliability and fix bugs</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do <strong>not</strong> use your data for advertising. We do
      <strong>not</strong> sell your data to third parties. We do
      <strong>not</strong> use your location history to build a profile
      of you.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Paw Watch relies on the following third-party services to operate.
      Each has its own privacy policy:
    </p>
    <dl>
      <dt>Supabase (backend)</dt>
      <dd>
        Stores your account, profile, reports, walk history, and
        notification tokens. Supabase's privacy policy:
        <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">supabase.com/privacy</a>.
      </dd>
      <dt>Google Maps</dt>
      <dd>
        Shows the map view and converts addresses to coordinates.
        Google's privacy policy:
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      </dd>
      <dt>Apple (Sign in with Apple, Push)</dt>
      <dd>
        Handles authentication and push delivery on iOS. Apple's
        privacy policy:
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">apple.com/legal/privacy</a>.
      </dd>
      <dt>Google (Sign in with Google)</dt>
      <dd>
        Handles authentication when you choose to sign in with
        Google. Google's privacy policy:
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      </dd>
      <dt>Expo (push notifications)</dt>
      <dd>
        Routes push notifications from our backend to Apple/Google.
        Expo's privacy policy:
        <a href="https://expo.dev/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">expo.dev/privacy</a>.
      </dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Paw Watch is not intended for children under 13. We do not
      knowingly collect information from children under 13. If you
      believe a child under 13 has created an account, please contact
      us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>

    <h3>Access, correction, and deletion</h3>
    <p>
      You can:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Update your profile</strong> (name, home location,
        alert radius) at any time in the Profile tab.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Delete your reports</strong> by tapping a report you
        submitted and selecting "Delete."
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Delete your account</strong> by contacting us at
        <a href="mailto:privacy@paw-watch.app">privacy@paw-watch.app</a>.
        We will delete your profile, reports, walks, and notification
        tokens within 30 days.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Export your data</strong> by contacting us at
        <a href="mailto:privacy@paw-watch.app">privacy@paw-watch.app</a>.
        We'll send you a JSON archive of your account within 30 days.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>California residents (CCPA / CPRA)</h3>
    <p>
      California residents have the right to know what personal
      information we collect, to delete it, and to opt out of any
      "sale" or "sharing." We do not sell or share personal information
      for cross-context behavioral advertising. To exercise your
      rights, contact
      <a href="mailto:privacy@paw-watch.app">privacy@paw-watch.app</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>European Union and United Kingdom (GDPR)</h3>
    <p>
      If you are in the EU or UK, our legal basis for processing your
      data is your consent (location, notifications) and the
      performance of our service (account, reports). You have the
      right to access, correct, delete, restrict, or port your data,
      and to lodge a complaint with your local data protection
      authority. To exercise your rights, contact
      <a href="mailto:privacy@paw-watch.app">privacy@paw-watch.app</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Active reports:</strong> 24 hours (low severity),
        72 hours (medium), or 7 days (high), then auto-expired.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Walk history:</strong> retained on your account until
        you delete it or delete your account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Account profile:</strong> retained until you delete
        your account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Push notification tokens:</strong> deleted when you
        sign out or delete your account.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use TLS for all data in transit. Data at rest is stored in
      Supabase's encrypted Postgres database. We follow industry
      practices for secrets management and access control. That said,
      no system is perfectly secure — if you believe your account has
      been compromised, contact us immediately.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we change this policy in a material way, we'll notify you
      through the app and update the "last updated" date above. If the
      changes are significant (e.g., a new category of data
      collection), we'll ask for your consent again.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Paw Watch is published by Cerminara Consulting LLC.
    </p>
    <dl class="contact">
      <dt>Email</dt>
      <dd><a href="mailto:privacy@paw-watch.app">privacy@paw-watch.app</a></dd>
      <dt>Mailing address</dt>
      <dd>
        Cerminara Consulting LLC<br />
        Attn: Paw Watch Privacy<br />
        Richmond, VA 23220<br />
        United States
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</Layout>
